= PKI CLI Connection =

By default PKI CLI will connect to the PKI server with the following parameters:
* Protocol: http
* Hostname: localhost
* Port: 8080
* Subsystem: ca

The parameters can be individually changed with the following options:
<pre>
$ pki -P <protocol> -h <hostname> -p <port> -t <subsystem> <command>
</pre>

Alternatively, the connection parameters can be specified as a URL:
<pre>
$ pki -U <URL> <command>
</pre>

In Dogtag 10.0.x the URL is in this format: https://&lt;hostname&gt;:&lt;port&gt;/&lt;subsystem&gt;.

Since Dogtag 10.1.x the URL is in this format: https://&lt;hostname&gt;:&lt;port&gt;. The subsystem will be determined by the command being executed.

For example, to access a local PKI server, no need to specify the connection parameters:

<pre>
$ pki ca-cert-find
</pre>

To access a remote PKI server:

<pre>
$ pki -h server.example.com ca-cert-find
</pre>

To access a remote PKI server using a secure connection:

<pre>
$ pki -U https://server.example.com:8443 ca-cert-find
</pre>

